  )
  :caveats ("Read the letters right to left after dropping c and r: dda means car then cdr then cdr." "cddar answers a LIST (a tail), because its leftmost letter is d." "(cddar '()) raises, and so does any input too shallow along this path. That is what R7RS-small 6.4.1 asks for: it defines cddar as (cdr (cdr (car pair))), and the chain raises at the first step that is not a pair. The error names cddar rather than a nested car or cdr." "The argument must be nested at least 3 deep along this exact path; a flat list of the right length is NOT enough." "An empty result is a legitimate answer here, not a failure -- it means the input had exactly enough to drop and nothing after.")
