     :problem "The operator is working with records with a two-field header and needs one fixed spot: dropping a two-field header off the first record. Candidates: cddar (one name, 3 steps, and the reader must decode the letters), the spelled-out chain (cdr (cdr (car x))) (identical on well-shaped input and correctly strict on everything else), or list-ref / list-tail when the depth is a number rather than a shape. For a path that is fixed at authoring time and short, cddar is the honest verb, and it raises when the shape is wrong exactly as the chain does."
